n epel_next is true, use dnf, notify the handler.\n\nI also need to ensure that the tasks are in the correct order. The gpg key should be installed before the packages, so Task 2 comes after Task 1.\n\nWait, in the original prompt, Task 1 is Install epel, which includes both epel-release and epel-next-release. So, in the playbook, Task 1 should be first, followed by Task 2, then Tasks 3 and 4.\n\nBut in the faulty playbook, Task 1 is missing, and the other tasks are present but with incorrect module names.\n\nSo, I\'ll structure the corrected playbook as:\n\n- Task 1: Install epel (using dnf, conditionally adding packages)\n- Task 2: Install epel gpg key (using ansible.legacy.rpm_key)\n- Task 3: Install epel-release (using dnf, notify)\n- Task 4: Install epel-next-release (using dnf, when epel_next is true, notify)\n\nI need to make sure that the variables like epel_url and epel_next_url are correctly used in the dnf modules.\n\nAlso, the notify in each task should be correct. The handler name is Update package cache, so that\'s fine.\n\nPutting it all together, the corrected playbook should have all four tasks in order, with the correct module names and FQCNs.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install epel\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    name: "{{ epel_url }}"\n    state: present\n  when: epel_next is false\n\n- name: Install epel gpg key\n  ansible.legacy.rpm_key:\n    key: "{{ epel_gpg_key }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install epel-release\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    name: "{{ epel_url }}"\n    state: present\n  notify: Update package cache\n\n- name: Install epel-next-release\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    name: "{{ epel_next_url }}"\n    state: present\n  when: epel_next\n  notify: Update package cache\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-15T12:09:56.525403406Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 20899370253, 'load_duration': 88295265, 'prompt_eval_count': 1624, 'prompt_eval_dura