y additional comments or explanations, keeping the YAML clean.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll start with the \'---\' line, then list each task in the specified order. Each task will have the correct module, parameters, and conditions. For the sysctl task, I\'ll add a condition to skip containers and a notify to reload the service if needed.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll write out the YAML accordingly, ensuring it\'s valid and meets all the user\'s requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Install requirements\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ sysctl_requirements }}"\n    state: present\n    update_cache: yes\n\n- name: Set sysctl setting\n  sysctl:\n    name: "{{ item.name }}"\n    value: "{{ item.value }}"\n    sysctl_set: "{{ sysctl_set }}"\n    sysctl_reload: "{{ sysctl_reload | default(\'yes\') | lower }}"\n  loop: "{{ sysctl_items }}"\n  when: not (ansible_connection in [\'container\', \'docker\', \'community.docker.docker\'])\n  notify: reload_sysctl\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\nhandlers:\n  - name: reload_sysctl\n    service:\n      name: sysctl\n      state: reload\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-15T12:55:19.67816984Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13401787229, 'load_duration': 92052952, 'prompt_eval_count': 433, 'prompt_eval_duration': 121863909, 'eval_count': 701, 'eval_duration': 13186510773, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--69aae27a-61ca-4501-97ec-23da54a69cf1-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 433, 'output_tokens': 701, 'total_tokens': 1134}
